{"key":"ics/T0847","id":"T0847","name":"Replication Through Removable Media","domain":"ics","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["initial-access"],"platforms":["None"],"environments":["ics-ot"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may move onto systems, such as those separated from the enterprise network, by copying malware to removable media which is inserted into the control systems environment. The adversary may rely on unknowing trusted third parties, such as suppliers or contractors with access privileges, to introduce the removable media. This technique enables initial access to target devices that never connect to untrusted networks, but are physically…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T0847","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--c267bbee-bb59-47fe-85e0-3ed210337c21","source_modified":"2025-04-15T19:59:04.946Z","source_object_version":"1.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0042","name":"Drive Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0042","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d6e6b3b-4aa8-40e1-8c47-91db0f313d9f","page":"telemetry/DC0042/"},{"id":"DC0055","name":"File Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0055","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--235b7491-2d2b-4617-9a52-3c0783680f71","page":"telemetry/DC0055/"},{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0733","name":"Detection of Replication Through Removable Media","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0733","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--cb273244-c117-4e32-afc7-f72f4e44e179","relationship_id":"relationship--0c145fb9-b67d-41ef-94a8-8bd3a5eabd3e"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN1866","name":"Analytic 1866","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0733#AN1866","guidance":"Monitor for newly executed processes that execute from removable media after it is mounted or when initiated by a user. If a remote access tool is used in this manner to move laterally, then additional actions are likely to occur after execution, such as opening network connections for Command and Control and system and network information Discovery. Monitor for newly constructed files copied to or from removable media. Monitor for newly constructed drive letters or mount points to removable media. Monitor for files accessed on removable media, particularly those with executable content.","platforms":["None"],"strategy_id":"DET0733"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"Process","channel":"None","platforms":["None"],"analytic_id":"AN1866","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0733#AN1866","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0039","component":"File Creation","name":"File","channel":"None","platforms":["None"],"analytic_id":"AN1866","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0733#AN1866","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"component_id":"DC0042","component":"Drive Creation","name":"Drive","channel":"None","platforms":["None"],"analytic_id":"AN1866","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0733#AN1866","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0042/"},{"component_id":"DC0055","component":"File Access","name":"File","channel":"None","platforms":["None"],"analytic_id":"AN1866","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0733#AN1866","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_valid